  "runner_up_case": "The entire ADVERSE case rests on one fact type: OFAC's 2025-09-16 designation of ALPA HONG KONG LIMITED as an SDN (IFSR; SDGT, E.O. 13224, via ownership/control by Alireza Derakhshan). The strongest honest case for NO_ADVERSE attacks its two load-bearing links. First, attachment/identity: the subject is 'Alpa Hong Kong Ltd' while the designated entity is 'ALPA HONG KONG LIMITED', and the name-to-number linkage (Company No. 3321489 / BRN 75743885) comes solely from OFAC's own listing — it was never verified against an independent registry record (no gleif or registry lookup was run; the Q1/Q7 phrasing 'as shown in the Hong Kong Companies Registry' overstates an ofac.treasury.gov source). If the subject is a distinct namesake, the sanctions do not attach to it. Second, currency: the designation is over a year old, every sanctions snippet in the record is undated, and the team's own sanctions-tool calls failed twice (UnusableArgument), so no working list query ever confirmed the entry is still live as of 2026-10-01. OFAC delistings via administrative reconsideration, settlement, or court order do occur, and the present-tense claim 'is sanctioned as of 2026-10-01' fails if the entry was removed. Honesty compels the caveat: an SDN designation is precisely the material adverse fact the rubric names, sourced from primary US government records, and NO_ADVERSE additionally requires a confirmed identity — so if the identity attack succeeded, the honest landing spot would be UNVERIFIABLE, not NO_ADVERSE. NO_ADVERSE is therefore reachable only on the narrow path of confirmed identity plus a pre-2026-10-01 delisting or rescission; absent either, ADVERSE stands and is the correct verdict.",
